<component>
  <section>
    <templateId root="1.3.6.1.4.1.19376.1.5.3.1.3.4"/>
    <code code="10164-2" codeSystem="2.16.840.1.113883.6.1" displayName="History of Present illness Narrative"/>
    <title>History of Present Illness</title>
    <text><paragraph>Mr. Rousseau returns for his yearly preventive visit, six months after a bulbar urethroplasty and five months into aripiprazole 5 mg. He passes urine with a free stream and has not used a sound or catheter since January. His back pain settled within three weeks. He sleeps six to seven hours. He still believes that some former friends speak against him, but he says the thought now occupies him for minutes rather than hours, and he writes most mornings. He has had no thoughts of suicide or of harming anyone. He completed the health risk assessment before the visit. [S]</paragraph><table><thead><tr><th>Element</th><th>Detail</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Visit</td><td>Adult preventive visit, age 55</td></tr><tr><td>Active conditions</td><td>Delusional disorder, persecutory type, on aripiprazole and completing CBT for psychosis; bulbar urethral stricture after urethroplasty; right inguinal hernia under watchful waiting</td></tr><tr><td>Medicines</td><td>Aripiprazole 5 mg each morning; acetaminophen as needed</td></tr><tr><td>Recent events</td><td>Low back strain in June, resolved</td></tr><tr><td>Functional status</td><td>Independent; walking two hours most days</td></tr></tbody></table><paragraph>Health risk assessment. Completed by the patient before the visit and reviewed during the visit. [S]</paragraph><table><thead><tr><th>Domain</th><th>Finding</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Self-rated health</td><td>Good, and better than for many years</td></tr><tr><td>Psychosocial</td><td>Lives with his long-term partner; sees few people by choice; no financial strain; feels safer at home than in the winter</td></tr><tr><td>Behavioral</td><td>Never smoker; a glass of wine with dinner a few times a week; walks and collects plants daily; plain diet with vegetables and bread</td></tr><tr><td>Activities of daily living</td><td>Independent in all</td></tr><tr><td>Instrumental activities of daily living</td><td>Manages his own medicines, money, correspondence, and household</td></tr><tr><td>Home safety</td><td>Smoke detector working; no firearms; no falls; wears a seat belt</td></tr><tr><td>Hearing and vision</td><td>Reading glasses; hearing normal</td></tr><tr><td>Sleep</td><td>Six to seven hours most nights</td></tr></tbody></table></text>

  </section>
</component>

