    <code code="51847-2" codeSystem="2.16.840.1.113883.6.1" displayName="Evaluation + Plan note"/>
    <title>Assessment and Plan</title>
    <text><list listType="ordered"><item><content styleCode="Bold">Adult preventive visit completed</content>. Health risk assessment reviewed and a written prevention plan given. Depression screen negative; AUDIT-C 1. [S]<list><item>Next preventive visit in one year.</item></list></item><item><content styleCode="Bold">Cardiovascular risk</content>. LDL cholesterol 126 mg/dL, total 201, HDL 47 two months ago; blood pressure 122/78; non-smoker; no diabetes. Estimated 10-year cardiovascular risk about 5 percent. [S]<list><item>No statin; diet and activity.</item><item>Lipids yearly on aripiprazole.</item></list></item><item><content styleCode="Bold">Right inguinal hernia (K40.90)</content>. Small, reducible, and painless, and no larger now that he no longer strains to pass urine. [S]<list><item>Continue watchful waiting; repair if it becomes painful or enlarges.</item><item>Warning signs of incarceration reviewed.</item></list></item></list><paragraph>Personalized prevention plan. A written copy was given to the patient. [S]</paragraph><table><thead><tr><th>Service</th><th>Status</th><th>Detail</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Influenza vaccine, 2026-2027</td><td>Completed today</td><td>Inactivated vaccine given today</td></tr><tr><td>Recombinant zoster vaccine</td><td>Completed today</td><td>Dose 1 today; dose 2 in two to six months</td></tr><tr><td>Pneumococcal vaccine</td><td>Completed today</td><td>PCV20 given today; recommended from age 50</td></tr><tr><td>COVID-19 vaccine, 2026-2027</td><td>Due</td><td>Recommended; he will consider it at the pharmacy</td></tr><tr><td>Hepatitis B vaccine</td><td>Due</td><td>Recommended for adults 19 to 59; to start once the screening result is back</td></tr><tr><td>Tetanus booster</td><td>Up to date</td><td>Tdap seven years ago</td></tr><tr><td>Colorectal cancer screening</td><td>Ordered</td><td>Never screened; after discussing colonoscopy and stool testing he chose a yearly fecal immunochemical test; kit given today</td></tr><tr><td>Prostate cancer screening (PSA)</td><td>Declined</td><td>Shared decision for men 55 to 69: benefits and harms explained; he chose not to have a PSA test now and will revisit next year</td></tr><tr><td>Hepatitis B, hepatitis C, and HIV screening</td><td>Ordered</td><td>One-time screening; no prior result on record; drawn today, results pending</td></tr><tr><td>Cholesterol screening and statin decision</td><td>Completed today</td><td>Lipids from the twelve-week aripiprazole check reviewed; 10-year risk about 5 percent; no statin</td></tr><tr><td>Diabetes screening</td><td>Up to date</td><td>Hemoglobin A1c 5.5 percent two months ago</td></tr><tr><td>Lung cancer screening</td><td>Not indicated</td><td>Never smoker</td></tr><tr><td>Blood pressure screening</td><td>Completed today</td><td>122/78 mmHg</td></tr><tr><td>Depression screening</td><td>Completed today</td><td>PHQ-2 score 0</td></tr><tr><td>Unhealthy alcohol use screening</td><td>Completed today</td><td>AUDIT-C 1, negative</td></tr><tr><td>Physical activity and diet counseling</td><td>Completed today</td><td>Keep walking daily; strength exercise twice a week; alcohol within one drink a day</td></tr></tbody></table><paragraph>Immunizations given today: Influenza vaccine, 2026-2027 season; Recombinant zoster vaccine, dose 1 of 2; Pneumococcal conjugate vaccine PCV20 [S]</paragraph><paragraph>Guideline basis: Medicare Preventive Services reference: visit templates, screening cascades, and documentation elements (2026); USPSTF A and B Recommendations (2026); Adult Immunization Schedule by Age (2026)</paragraph><paragraph>Follow-up: Hepatitis B, hepatitis C, and HIV results by letter, as he asked. Return the stool test kit within two weeks. Second zoster dose in two to six months. Six-month urology review and aripiprazole review as booked. [S]</paragraph></text>

  </section>
